\subsection{F7: Full-Pathway Gradient Stopping Eliminates CIVO}
\label{sec:f7}

Exp\_018 applies full-pathway selective gradient stopping (SGS), detaching all non-KL gradients from the temporal embedding $e_{\dt}$ so that only the KL dynamics signal remains (7.3\% of gradient flow at convergence). Under the same configuration that produces catastrophic CIVO in exp\_008d (trained $e_{\dt}$, $d{=}32$, subsample ON, $H{=}8$, $\dt{=}2$ imagination), exp\_018 \sgsclaim{}: NVE remains at $\sgsnve{}\times$ throughout the 35K+ diagnostic window (vs.\ $4.12\times$ for 008d), with no pathological collapse. Evaluation reaches \sgseval{} at 105K (49\% of baseline), compared to 008d's 82.8 (9\% of baseline).

This result enables a decomposition of the total degradation. The 008d configuration suffers 86\% degradation from baseline; exp\_018 reduces this to 51\%. The 35-percentage-point difference isolates CIVO's independent contribution, separating it from the inherent cost of $\dt{=}2$ imagination. Full-pathway SGS downgrades catastrophic pathological collapse to moderate variable-rate cost.

The progression across gradient-stopping interventions establishes a monotonic relationship between gradient removal and CIVO suppression:
\begin{itemize}[nosep,leftmargin=*]
\item Exp\_016e (reward-only SGS): NVE $10.42\times$, collapse to 31.7---functionally insufficient since the reward head's gradient contribution diminishes to negligible levels at convergence.
\item Exp\_018 (full-pathway SGS, removing 92.7\% of converged gradient flow): NVE $\sgsnve{}\times$, eval \sgseval{}---CIVO eliminated, inherent $\dt{=}2$ cost remains.
\item Exp\_008f (embedding removed, 100\% removal): NVE $0.97\times$, eval 503.0---no CIVO, but lower performance due to loss of all temporal information.
\end{itemize}

